    ("EventSubscribedCodes", 'Event', "result", (("ptr:int32", "OutCodes"), ("size", "Capacity"), ("ptr:int32", "OutWritten"), ),
     "Which NOTIFY_* codes this slot is subscribed to, into the caller's buffer. EventSubscribe and EventUnsubscribe could change that table since ABI 12 and nothing could read it, so a payload swapped in beside another one could not tell what it had inherited. MAXMCP_FACADE_TOO_LARGE with OutWritten set, the contract every list read here has. Only entries whose Holders is non-zero are reported, because EventUnsubscribe zeroes Code on the last release (src/the slot's own source:3582) - so code 0 is unrepresentable in this table and a payload cannot use this entry to prove it is NOT subscribed to code 0. This is the EventSubscribe table and NOT the callback DECLARATION table that superseded it (src/the slot's own source:3405-3407): two mechanisms, and folding them would be the slot deciding they are the same thing. AN EMPTY TABLE ANSWERS OK, NOT TOO_LARGE, whatever OutCodes and Capacity are, and ShapeSplinePointsRead answers the same way for an empty spline - the reasoning is written out at that entry.", 'the event queue, readable'),
